  {
    "insert": "\t\t\tThe language in scientific work should be precise, formal, and objective to communicate ideas clearly and credibly, without trying the reader to convince. However, in this proposal there are some areas where the language could be further refined. For example avoid using “we”, “our”. Instead, consider make it more neutral, objective. I recommend reviewing the text to eliminate subjective language. \n(Language)"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\t\t\tIn general, using long sentences could make the ideas harder to understand for readers. It is highly recommended to use short and understandable sentences. For example in the second paragraph of the motivation the sentences could be separated into more clear and short ones. On the other hand, there are a lot of short paragraphs, which could be added to each other. Try to use shorter sentences and edit the paragraphs.\n(Hook)"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
